"Paul E Collins" <find_my_real_address@CL4.org> wrote:

>In defaults.nh I have:
>OPTIONS=name:Eq,role:Wizard,race:gnome,gender:female,align:neutral
>
>When I start NetHack (3.4.2, Windows) the dialogue shows wizard, *orc* 
>(not gnome), female, and neutral, and then rejects the selection 
>because of "incompatible alignment".

It works correctly in 3.4.3. The bug may be related to an issue fixed
from 3.4.2 to 3.4.3: "win32gui: you couldn't specify an alignment in
defaults.nh and have it stick". If you are forced to stick with 3.4.2,
run nethack.exe instead of nethackw.exe and see whether it works (The
fixed bug seems to be specific to the GUI version.).

